==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|uptaken|t=to take up, lift}}, partial calque of earlier {{der|en|enm|upnimen|t=to take up, lift}}, equivalent to {{pre|en|up|take}}. Compare {{cog|sv|upptaga}}, {{m|sv|uppta|t=to take up}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{q|noun}} {{IPA|en|/ˈʌpteɪk/}}
** {{audio|en|en-us-uptake.ogg|a=US}}
* {{q|verb}} {{IPA|en|/ʌpˈteɪk/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# [[understanding|Understanding]]; [[comprehension]].
# [[absorption|Absorption]], especially of [[food]] or [[nutrient]] by an [[organism]].
# The act of lifting or taking up.
# {{lb|en|dated}} A [[chimney]].
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1951|month=January|title=Notes and News: New Roof for Cricklewood M.P.D.|journal=Railway Magazine|page=67|text=The design provides for continuous smoke troughs of reinforced concrete, vented by circular '''uptakes''', and the turntable area will be covered, using precast reinforced concrete bars down both sides of each track.}}
# {{lb|en|dated}} The [[upcast]] [[pipe]] from the [[smokebox]] of a [[steam boiler]] towards the [[chimney]].

====Derived terms====
* {{l|en|on the uptake}}
* {{l|en|quick on the uptake}}
* {{l|en|slow on the uptake}}
* {{l|en|reuptake}}

